{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>ההרימו</b> — The heh is the one that enters upon transitive verbs, like <b>ההליכא</b> (the sending away), <b>השבה</b> (the returning). And the reason is <b>אשר</b>.</b>"], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Aramaic-style forms with definite-article heh prefixed to verbs; the citation אשר likely refers to the accent/ta'am governing the form. The lemma ההליכוא appears with a vav in some witnesses; translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:17.262802023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}